      "hints": [
        "Find $a = S_1 = 5$ and $u_2 = S_2 - S_1 = 7 \\implies d = 2$.",
        "Express $u_k = 2k + 3 > 200$.",
        "Solve for smallest integer $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the first term $a$ and common difference $d$ using $S_n = n^2 + 4n$:\n$$a = S_1 = 1^2 + 4(1) = 5$$\n$$S_2 = 2^2 + 4(2) = 12 \\implies u_2 = S_2 - S_1 = 12 - 5 = 7$$\n$$d = u_2 - u_1 = 7 - 5 = 2$$",
        "Express the $k$th term $u_k$ using the formula $u_k = a + (k - 1)d$:\n$$u_k = 5 + (k - 1)(2) = 2k + 3$$",
        "Set up the inequality for the $k$th term exceeding $200$:\n$$2k + 3 > 200 \\implies 2k > 197 \\implies k > 98.5$$",
        "State the smallest integer value of $k$:\n$$k = 99$$"
      ],
